1
00:00:46,671 --> 00:00:48,089
Take it easy.

2
00:00:51,718 --> 00:00:53,053
Mr. Attorney.

3
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:55,263
Can you hear me, Mr. Attorney?

4
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:57,682
Attorney Byeon!

5
00:00:58,558 --> 00:00:59,684
Yeah, what is it?

6
00:00:59,768 --> 00:01:01,269
They're using a lot of ammo up here.

7
00:01:03,438 --> 00:01:05,482
Do they expect me to get hit and die?

8
00:01:05,565 --> 00:01:06,441
No, Sang-ung.

9
00:01:06,524 --> 00:01:08,860
They're merely trying
to restrict your liquidity.

10
00:01:11,362 --> 00:01:12,947
Well, I'm used to being broke by now.

11
00:01:13,031 --> 00:01:14,157
I'm almost there.

12
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:16,659
Just hold on a little longer. Okay.

13
00:02:51,421 --> 00:02:53,173
When you neutralize the henchmen,

14
00:02:53,256 --> 00:02:54,841
come into the branch manager's office.

15
00:02:56,176 --> 00:02:57,051
MANAGER'S OFFICE

16
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:01,055
Through there, we can get
straight into the secret vault.

17
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:03,975
Once everything's ready,
I'll lower you down.

18
00:03:20,325 --> 00:03:21,618
Seriously?

19
00:03:24,579 --> 00:03:26,497
Hey. Bun-mi? Help, please!

20
00:03:29,459 --> 00:03:31,211
Give me a second.

21
00:03:46,309 --> 00:03:48,186
GIMHAE SAVINGS BANK

22
00:03:57,946 --> 00:04:00,490
You either get Sang-ung
and bring him to me or die trying.

23
00:04:00,573 --> 00:04:02,033
Yes, ma'am!

24
00:04:39,737 --> 00:04:41,781
-I think I'm gonna puke.
-Hey.

25
00:04:44,534 --> 00:04:45,952
You took your sweet time.

26
00:04:46,035 --> 00:04:47,870
What? Wish I'd taken longer.

27
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:50,248
-First, find Kang Sang-ung.
-They're here.

28
00:04:58,881 --> 00:05:01,926
We'll get the Mundane Vanguard
to fight Jo Anna's crew.

29
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:05,221
They'll be too tied up with each other
to chase after us.

30
00:05:05,305 --> 00:05:07,015
And that way we'll be alone,

31
00:05:07,515 --> 00:05:08,516
in the secret vault.

32
00:05:10,685 --> 00:05:13,187
Mr. Attorney, do you copy?
We're heading to the office, all right?

33
00:05:17,567 --> 00:05:19,319
It's not safe.

34
00:05:20,778 --> 00:05:23,031
Attorney Byeon. Please respond.

35
00:05:23,114 --> 00:05:24,073
There's no signal.

36
00:05:24,824 --> 00:05:25,992
We better hurry.

37
00:05:41,299 --> 00:05:42,508
We have to get down there fast.

38
00:06:22,673 --> 00:06:23,883
Attorney Byeon?

39
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,385
Byeon, can you hear me?

40
00:06:27,887 --> 00:06:29,138
Attorney Byeon?

41
00:06:31,349 --> 00:06:33,393
Attorney Byeon, are you okay?

42
00:07:21,190 --> 00:07:23,526
You never cease to amaze. Very impressive.

43
00:07:26,070 --> 00:07:29,323
No matter which way you look at it,
your superpower is the greatest.

44
00:07:32,702 --> 00:07:33,786
The greatest,

45
00:07:34,454 --> 00:07:35,955
as long as you have enough money.

46
00:07:48,509 --> 00:07:50,428
I'll shut you up with what I have here.

47
00:07:55,766 --> 00:07:58,478
Here's a fun drug
we'll be releasing when it's ready.

48
00:08:01,939 --> 00:08:02,899
Hey.

49
00:08:03,483 --> 00:08:05,860
What are you getting out of all this?
Why go this far?

50
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:07,487
Well, money, of course.

51
00:08:07,570 --> 00:08:09,864
When I finally take control
of your superpower,

52
00:08:09,947 --> 00:08:11,657
I'll need as much money as I can get.

53
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,592
REPLENISH YOUR CALORIES!

54
00:08:33,012 --> 00:08:34,555
That's all you got?

55
00:08:36,140 --> 00:08:37,725
How anticlimactic.

56
00:08:40,937 --> 00:08:43,147
What do you say, old-timer?
Should we call it quits?

57
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:54,575
Not a chance.

58
00:08:55,117 --> 00:08:56,827
Min-suk has something fun to tell me.

59
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:58,704
I plan on hearing it.

60
00:09:29,610 --> 00:09:31,696
Wrong way!

61
00:09:44,500 --> 00:09:46,085
Is it last call yet?

62
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,095
Attorney Byeon!

63
00:09:56,596 --> 00:09:57,847
Bun-mi!

64
00:09:57,930 --> 00:09:59,223
Hey, can you hear me?

65
00:09:59,307 --> 00:10:01,100
Attorney Byeon, can you hear me?

66
00:10:09,734 --> 00:10:11,569
What a horrible smell.

67
00:10:15,114 --> 00:10:18,534
I couldn't see it yet,
but I knew what it was.

68
00:10:19,952 --> 00:10:22,288
It was an oddly familiar stench.

69
00:10:22,788 --> 00:10:26,751
Like something I'd always dreamed about
but could never touch.

70
00:10:28,294 --> 00:10:31,213
And that horrible smell is…

71
00:10:35,676 --> 00:10:36,636
money.

72
00:10:45,186 --> 00:10:47,438
What's so funny?
You know we're about to die, right?

73
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,028
GIMHAE BANK
UNDERGROUND VAULT

74
00:10:55,404 --> 00:10:57,823
What do you think
is on the other side of that wall?

75
00:10:58,324 --> 00:10:59,617
Sewer line?

76
00:11:02,244 --> 00:11:05,331
You might think so from the rotten smell,
but that's not it.

77
00:11:06,499 --> 00:11:07,792
What are you saying?

78
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:12,171
According to the blueprints,

79
00:11:12,254 --> 00:11:16,008
this room is supposed to be 17 meters long
and 11 meters wide.

80
00:11:18,552 --> 00:11:20,680
Don't you agree
there's some space missing?

81
00:12:12,690 --> 00:12:14,150
It's true what they say.

82
00:12:15,067 --> 00:12:16,944
Money really does give you confidence.

83
00:12:28,164 --> 00:12:28,998
Still here?

84
00:12:32,626 --> 00:12:34,128
Look who it is.

85
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:35,463
Huh.

86
00:12:35,546 --> 00:12:36,756
Grandpa's alive.

87
00:12:40,843 --> 00:12:42,595
I told you not to call me that.

88
00:12:47,016 --> 00:12:49,101
So that's where he stashed it.

89
00:12:58,694 --> 00:13:01,113
Your old man's hiding
one hell of a piggy bank.

90
00:13:05,743 --> 00:13:08,579
Bun-mi, help Byeon outside.

91
00:13:08,662 --> 00:13:10,915
Now that we're finally face-to-face,

92
00:13:12,166 --> 00:13:13,876
I wanna say goodbye to our friend here.

93
00:13:14,543 --> 00:13:16,879
What a relief. Let's go, Bun-mi.

94
00:13:56,335 --> 00:13:58,879
I always knew money could fix my problems.

95
00:13:58,963 --> 00:14:01,215
But this is a whole other level.

96
00:15:00,357 --> 00:15:01,609
That's quite the power you have.

97
00:15:05,571 --> 00:15:06,739
It's worth every last cent.

98
00:15:07,907 --> 00:15:10,409
But what good is strength if you're blind?

99
00:15:27,676 --> 00:15:29,053
I see everything.

100
00:15:30,054 --> 00:15:31,263
Now say goodbye.

101
00:15:57,998 --> 00:15:59,249
Can you take my best shot?

102
00:16:28,779 --> 00:16:29,697
Huh?

103
00:16:33,993 --> 00:16:34,910
What?

104
00:16:43,085 --> 00:16:45,337
What the hell's going on?

105
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:50,843
This feels like waking up
after getting blackout drunk.

106
00:17:07,109 --> 00:17:09,611
I can't seem to use my superpowers.

107
00:17:16,326 --> 00:17:17,202
What the…

108
00:17:17,286 --> 00:17:20,289
Don't worry. We're not taking you away.

109
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:22,624
Sit tight.

110
00:17:38,974 --> 00:17:40,434
What the hell is he doing?

111
00:17:40,517 --> 00:17:41,685
Nothing good.

112
00:17:46,106 --> 00:17:47,357
Get out.

113
00:17:47,441 --> 00:17:49,943
I'm sure you'll behave
now that your superpowers are gone.

114
00:17:50,027 --> 00:17:51,111
Sorry?

115
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:53,572
-Get out of the car already.
-Hold on, wait! Hear me out.

116
00:17:56,658 --> 00:17:57,618
Jo Nathan.

117
00:17:58,118 --> 00:18:00,287
He's selling drugs that give superpowers.

118
00:18:01,163 --> 00:18:02,206
I'll look into it.

119
00:18:02,289 --> 00:18:04,500
You won't just look into it.
Go lock up that psycho.

120
00:18:10,089 --> 00:18:11,298
Didn't I tell you

121
00:18:11,381 --> 00:18:13,759
your actions could end up
hurting innocent people?

122
00:18:16,428 --> 00:18:18,305
So you're saying this is my fault.

123
00:18:18,931 --> 00:18:20,557
I mean, what do you expect me to do?

124
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,227
Just sit back and do nothing
while innocent people are getting hurt?

125
00:18:23,310 --> 00:18:26,063
You think this is the first time
the world's been in danger?

126
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,775
Listen, kid, there hasn't been
a single instant when it hasn't.

127
00:18:29,858 --> 00:18:31,985
There have always been thugs
like the Mundane Vanguard,

128
00:18:32,069 --> 00:18:33,362
putting new drugs on the streets.

129
00:18:34,571 --> 00:18:36,907
This fight started
before either of us were born,

130
00:18:36,990 --> 00:18:39,660
and it'll keep going
long after we're dead.

131
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:44,540
There are more ways to fight back
than you think.

132
00:18:44,623 --> 00:18:46,333
And a lot more people doing the fighting.

133
00:18:46,416 --> 00:18:48,585
-Now get out of here.
-Please listen to me.

134
00:18:51,672 --> 00:18:53,423
Come on, let's go! I'm getting hungry.

135
00:19:13,819 --> 00:19:16,655
GIMHAE SAVINGS BANK

136
00:19:28,083 --> 00:19:29,835
Get these ampoules into storage.

137
00:19:29,918 --> 00:19:30,836
Yes, ma'am.

138
00:19:36,341 --> 00:19:38,468
-And Lee Su-eun?
-I'm afraid she's still missing.

139
00:19:38,552 --> 00:19:39,970
I want her captured right away.

140
00:19:51,106 --> 00:19:52,065
Wow.

141
00:20:12,878 --> 00:20:14,713
What are you doing down here?

142
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,344
Drop your guns.

143
00:20:24,973 --> 00:20:27,517
Damn, it's hot under these.

144
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,913
Thanks to my son-in-law,

145
00:20:47,996 --> 00:20:49,957
I finally get to see inside this place.

146
00:20:51,583 --> 00:20:53,210
Who the hell are you, lady?

147
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,965
You must be Jo Won-do's daughter.

148
00:20:58,048 --> 00:20:59,633
You're the spitting image of your father.

149
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:02,386
I don't agree.

150
00:21:04,096 --> 00:21:07,140
Don't try anything stupid now.
Just stay nice and still.

151
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:11,270
I have no business here with you.

152
00:21:41,633 --> 00:21:44,511
You went on a rampage,
fighting with someone else's money,

153
00:21:44,594 --> 00:21:45,887
then passed out.

154
00:21:45,971 --> 00:21:47,931
And when you regained consciousness,

155
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,143
your powers were gone, is that right?

156
00:21:52,102 --> 00:21:52,936
Yeah.

157
00:21:56,815 --> 00:21:57,941
You're maxed out, son.

158
00:21:58,900 --> 00:22:00,986
I never get a straight answer
from this guy.

159
00:22:01,069 --> 00:22:02,529
Am I some kind of credit card now?

160
00:22:02,612 --> 00:22:03,780
What?

161
00:22:03,864 --> 00:22:06,366
I'm saying you don't have the capacity
to handle your superpowers.

162
00:22:09,453 --> 00:22:11,580
Kang Sang-ung, stay with me, okay?

163
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,464
Don't use other people's money.

164
00:22:20,547 --> 00:22:22,674
It's one of the first things I told you.

165
00:22:22,758 --> 00:22:24,468
Hang on. You… you gotta be…

166
00:22:24,551 --> 00:22:26,303
When you said
not to use other people's money,

167
00:22:26,386 --> 00:22:29,681
it seemed like you were giving
financial advice, not a steadfast rule.

168
00:22:33,560 --> 00:22:35,354
If my powers are gone,

169
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:37,481
when do they return?

170
00:22:37,981 --> 00:22:39,191
Who knows?

171
00:22:40,901 --> 00:22:43,278
It's just like with anything else in life.

172
00:22:43,362 --> 00:22:45,197
You can't let yourself get greedy.

173
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:48,283
Whether it's money, food, or alcohol.

174
00:22:48,867 --> 00:22:52,162
The second you try to go
beyond your limits, you land in trouble.

175
00:22:54,998 --> 00:22:56,416
The game is rigged.

176
00:22:57,334 --> 00:22:59,544
This was never a fair fight to begin with.

177
00:23:01,421 --> 00:23:03,924
If I have to use my own money,
and they're really fucking strong,

178
00:23:04,007 --> 00:23:05,801
then I never stood a chance at all!

179
00:23:06,301 --> 00:23:09,930
You could've passed this thing down
with some cash if you knew how it worked!

180
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:11,765
Listen, son.

181
00:23:11,848 --> 00:23:13,433
This isn't about the money.

182
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:15,477
What do you mean?
Of course that's what it's about!

183
00:23:15,560 --> 00:23:17,020
Only a moron could think otherwise.

184
00:23:17,104 --> 00:23:18,522
What if your power has disappeared?

185
00:23:18,605 --> 00:23:19,731
I…

186
00:23:20,774 --> 00:23:21,983
You would let them win?

187
00:23:23,902 --> 00:23:28,740
You'd let the Vanguard take your friends
all because you lost a lousy superpower?

188
00:23:32,285 --> 00:23:34,871
You were willing to do
what most people wouldn't.

189
00:23:35,580 --> 00:23:37,207
They wouldn't have used
their mother's gift

190
00:23:37,290 --> 00:23:39,543
to save a bus of complete strangers.

191
00:23:39,626 --> 00:23:42,254
The superpower wasn't
what saved those people.

192
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:44,131
It wasn't the cash either.

193
00:23:44,214 --> 00:23:45,424
It was you.

194
00:24:10,574 --> 00:24:12,325
Take some time to think about it.

195
00:24:14,494 --> 00:24:15,829
You might find out,

196
00:24:17,205 --> 00:24:19,207
the money isn't what gives you strength.

197
00:24:21,251 --> 00:24:22,711
When you're in the fight…

198
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:32,929
…when you're protecting others…

199
00:24:36,308 --> 00:24:38,477
there comes a moment of realization.

200
00:24:42,481 --> 00:24:45,317
You realize
the money isn't that important.

201
00:24:51,740 --> 00:24:53,158
You figure that out,

202
00:24:53,241 --> 00:24:55,744
and you'll have your powers back
in no time.

203
00:25:48,630 --> 00:25:50,090
THE MUNDANE VANGUARD

204
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:54,761
Shit.

205
00:26:06,481 --> 00:26:08,984
The extent of that loser's superpowers

206
00:26:09,484 --> 00:26:11,194
proved more than you could handle.

207
00:26:31,381 --> 00:26:33,300
Having to live with your failure

208
00:26:33,383 --> 00:26:35,343
is a punishment
that is far worse than death.

209
00:26:37,345 --> 00:26:39,431
It's funny how pride works.

210
00:26:39,514 --> 00:26:42,017
If you lose it, you lose everything.

211
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:05,332
Chairman.

212
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:07,542
JO ANNA

213
00:27:09,461 --> 00:27:10,795
What is it now?

214
00:27:11,296 --> 00:27:13,006
There are two things in this world

215
00:27:13,089 --> 00:27:16,301
no one has ever been able
to keep me from getting my hands on.

216
00:27:16,384 --> 00:27:18,386
BORROWER: JO SIN-IL
LENDER: PARK HYEONG-DO

217
00:27:19,471 --> 00:27:20,722
The cash owed on a debt,

218
00:27:21,431 --> 00:27:22,599
and the truth.

219
00:27:25,268 --> 00:27:27,354
Sorry to let you down,
but I don't owe any debt.

220
00:27:27,937 --> 00:27:29,773
That's not what
the ledger I'm holding says.

221
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:35,528
It's taken me a long time
to uncover your dirty little secret.

222
00:27:39,908 --> 00:27:42,869
Your empire may have taken
a century to build…

223
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:47,707
but it can all come crashing down
in the blink of an eye.

224
00:27:49,959 --> 00:27:52,629
You should know
I'm not as forgiving as my father was.

225
00:27:54,714 --> 00:27:58,927
I suggest you cough up the cash you owe,
or your health could suffer.

226
00:28:06,476 --> 00:28:08,228
Your phone, little girl.

227
00:28:10,939 --> 00:28:12,649
You're gonna regret this.

228
00:28:13,233 --> 00:28:14,109
Oh, really?

229
00:28:14,609 --> 00:28:18,405
I'd watch my mouth
before you find out what regret is.

230
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:22,242
I'll keep this money safe.
You can tell your father that.

231
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:23,535
Take it away.

232
00:28:23,618 --> 00:28:24,911
Yes, ma'am!

233
00:28:46,558 --> 00:28:49,227
Having superpowers is a major pain.

234
00:28:49,310 --> 00:28:50,437
But having them taken away

235
00:28:50,520 --> 00:28:53,106
right when you're starting
to get the hang of them,

236
00:28:53,982 --> 00:28:56,234
somehow, that's even worse.

237
00:29:15,003 --> 00:29:15,920
Min-suk?

238
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:22,761
Min-suk?

239
00:29:25,764 --> 00:29:27,015
Hey, Min-suk!

240
00:29:28,099 --> 00:29:29,184
Hey, Min…

241
00:29:30,351 --> 00:29:31,352
Min-suk!

242
00:29:48,578 --> 00:29:50,205
Oh shit.

243
00:29:52,207 --> 00:29:54,834
-Uh, hello--
-I was touched by what you said earlier.

244
00:29:59,547 --> 00:30:00,590
Where is Min-suk?

245
00:30:09,891 --> 00:30:11,726
I'm here, Sang-ung. I'm fine.

246
00:30:12,811 --> 00:30:14,062
Don't worry about me.

247
00:30:15,855 --> 00:30:16,773
Hey, Min-suk.

248
00:30:17,273 --> 00:30:18,274
Are you all right?

249
00:30:18,942 --> 00:30:21,569
Uh, just hold on a little longer.
I'll be right there.

250
00:30:22,153 --> 00:30:24,364
Why do you keep making things
more difficult?

251
00:30:27,617 --> 00:30:28,910
Listen, let's figure this out.

252
00:30:29,869 --> 00:30:31,454
You already know what I want.

253
00:30:32,497 --> 00:30:34,040
Fine, then, I'll come to you.

254
00:30:34,749 --> 00:30:35,875
Just leave Min-suk out--

255
00:30:38,002 --> 00:30:39,712
Hey. Hey! Hey!

256
00:30:39,796 --> 00:30:41,381
Hey, you motherfucker!

257
00:30:41,464 --> 00:30:43,424
I said I'd come. I'm coming right now!

258
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:54,060
I decide when.

259
00:30:55,436 --> 00:30:57,063
You just wait quietly.

260
00:31:01,860 --> 00:31:02,861
Shit. Come on.

261
00:31:04,195 --> 00:31:06,781
The person
you are trying to reach is unavailable…

262
00:31:16,374 --> 00:31:18,209
You really think you're gonna win,
don't you?

263
00:31:19,210 --> 00:31:21,713
You don't have what it takes
to beat Kang Sang-ung.

264
00:31:22,380 --> 00:31:23,840
What makes you so sure?

265
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:27,760
Because Sang-ung…

266
00:31:30,305 --> 00:31:32,223
is terrible at calculations.

267
00:31:33,558 --> 00:31:37,186
In the end, he always chooses
to do what he thinks is right,

268
00:31:37,270 --> 00:31:38,855
no matter how impossible

269
00:31:38,938 --> 00:31:40,481
or how much he'll get hurt.

270
00:31:40,565 --> 00:31:42,150
Ah, I see.

271
00:31:42,734 --> 00:31:45,320
So that's why
that little loser is always broke.

272
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:48,197
No. Sang-ung was broke to begin with.

273
00:31:51,200 --> 00:31:53,870
Why would you choose
a pushover like that guy?

274
00:31:53,953 --> 00:31:55,246
He thinks he's a saint.

275
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:57,248
Yeah, but you've got it wrong.

276
00:31:58,249 --> 00:32:00,919
That pushover is the one
who is putting up with me.

277
00:32:01,002 --> 00:32:04,547
And I should warn you
that he's not a pushover for anyone else.

278
00:32:05,632 --> 00:32:06,466
How touching.

279
00:32:06,549 --> 00:32:08,760
Damn right, it's touching. I married him!

280
00:32:11,554 --> 00:32:12,722
From where I sit,

281
00:32:12,805 --> 00:32:15,099
it feels like you're trying
to take my husband away from me.

282
00:32:16,184 --> 00:32:18,269
You ruined our dinner with the in-laws.

283
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:20,813
Now, we can't even have our wedding!

284
00:32:26,986 --> 00:32:28,237
Just you wait and see.

285
00:32:29,405 --> 00:32:30,573
You're gonna lose.

286
00:32:31,074 --> 00:32:33,117
We'll see who makes it out of this.

287
00:32:54,931 --> 00:32:56,265
Nobody move!

288
00:33:15,535 --> 00:33:18,162
Jo Nathan. He's selling drugs
that give superpowers.

289
00:33:18,246 --> 00:33:19,497
I'll look into it.

290
00:33:19,580 --> 00:33:21,582
You won't just look into it.
Go lock up that psycho.

291
00:33:28,464 --> 00:33:31,759
Why'd we go all the way out to Gimhae
to let him go first chance we get?

292
00:33:32,343 --> 00:33:33,970
What's really going on here?

293
00:33:38,141 --> 00:33:40,601
Kang Sang-ung. Why isn't he under arrest?

294
00:33:43,104 --> 00:33:44,856
'Cause he hadn't committed a crime.

295
00:33:47,692 --> 00:33:50,403
And since when did we start letting people
who break into safes go?

296
00:33:54,407 --> 00:33:55,491
Look, guys.

297
00:33:55,575 --> 00:33:58,286
There's one thing more valuable
than cash in this world.

298
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:00,038
Know what it is?

299
00:34:01,372 --> 00:34:02,290
What?

300
00:34:04,751 --> 00:34:05,960
It's time.

301
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:11,632
We never have enough of it,
and you couldn't buy even it if you tried.

302
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:41,788
You look great.

303
00:34:52,298 --> 00:34:54,133
Don't be late next time.

304
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:42,473
Min-suk, where is she?

305
00:35:42,557 --> 00:35:45,434
We'll get to that.
You need to pass a test first.

306
00:35:59,282 --> 00:36:00,533
What kind of test?

307
00:36:00,616 --> 00:36:02,660
I heard in the safe you passed out.

308
00:36:03,161 --> 00:36:05,037
If it's true you lost your power,

309
00:36:05,121 --> 00:36:07,331
then I think it's best
if everybody moves on.

310
00:36:09,417 --> 00:36:11,169
That's when it hit me.

311
00:36:11,836 --> 00:36:13,504
If I don't have my superpowers,

312
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:17,049
it means I'm completely useless to them.

313
00:36:22,221 --> 00:36:23,639
If you take me down,

314
00:36:24,140 --> 00:36:25,600
I'll take you to your girl.

315
00:36:26,934 --> 00:36:28,144
But if you're impotent…

316
00:36:33,649 --> 00:36:35,234
you and your little girly,

317
00:36:35,985 --> 00:36:37,486
your days are numbered.

318
00:36:38,946 --> 00:36:40,198
I'm sorry to say,

319
00:36:40,948 --> 00:36:43,284
there's something fun
that Min-suk wanted to share.

320
00:36:44,702 --> 00:36:46,454
So I think I'll stay above ground.

321
00:37:52,019 --> 00:37:53,020
Min-suk.

322
00:37:54,772 --> 00:37:55,815
Where is she?

323
00:38:39,275 --> 00:38:40,651
Are you okay?

324
00:38:40,735 --> 00:38:42,820
What happened to seeing everything?

325
00:38:52,621 --> 00:38:54,582
Where is Min-suk?

326
00:38:58,753 --> 00:39:00,629
Tell me where you're holding her.

327
00:39:09,055 --> 00:39:11,474
You really have lost your powers.

328
00:39:13,476 --> 00:39:15,603
It looks like both of you are dead.

329
00:39:15,686 --> 00:39:17,480
My fight isn't with you.

330
00:39:21,859 --> 00:39:22,818
Just tell me.

331
00:39:25,321 --> 00:39:26,405
Min-suk.

332
00:39:27,907 --> 00:39:29,116
Where is she?

333
00:39:31,827 --> 00:39:32,870
You'll see her in hell.

334
00:40:06,404 --> 00:40:09,031
One more step, you'll be Swiss cheese.

335
00:40:56,787 --> 00:40:59,665
DIVORCE ATTORNEY BYEON HO-IN

336
00:41:03,085 --> 00:41:05,004
BEOMHA LOGISTICS

337
00:41:05,087 --> 00:41:06,088
Here it is.

338
00:41:15,014 --> 00:41:16,390
BEOMHA LOGISTICS
FIRST FLOOR

339
00:41:16,474 --> 00:41:19,935
The Mundane Vanguard has thugs
watching every entrance into the building.

340
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:21,228
HORIZONTAL CROSS SECTION

341
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,397
You can bet they're watching Min-suk too.

342
00:41:24,899 --> 00:41:27,109
Going in now would be a suicide mission.

343
00:41:33,991 --> 00:41:37,036
You would accomplish nothing,
and we will all be dead!

344
00:41:38,537 --> 00:41:40,164
It'd be a long shot,
even with your powers.

345
00:41:40,247 --> 00:41:41,749
When we first met,

346
00:41:42,750 --> 00:41:44,960
you asked why I helped those people.

347
00:41:45,461 --> 00:41:46,795
The bus accident.

348
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,506
Remember?

349
00:41:53,677 --> 00:41:56,514
I did it because I had to.
There was no other choice.

350
00:41:57,556 --> 00:41:59,600
With superpowers or without,

351
00:42:00,267 --> 00:42:01,477
I'd still try.

352
00:42:05,648 --> 00:42:08,108
Using belief alone
won't get you out alive.

353
00:42:08,192 --> 00:42:11,237
Listen to my warnings.
I ran all the calculations, Sang-ung!

354
00:42:20,871 --> 00:42:22,665
I'm terrible at calculations.

355
00:42:46,188 --> 00:42:49,984
BEOMHA LOGISTICS

356
00:43:22,099 --> 00:43:24,852
I think I understand
what my dad was trying to say.

357
00:43:26,270 --> 00:43:27,563
My strength

358
00:43:28,105 --> 00:43:29,607
